Dataclass EvalModelRef:
- carry one provider/model pair for the local evaluation matrix
- expose a stable label string for report grouping

Dataclass EvalSeedRun:
- describe the optional seed run used before a follow-up case
- keep the seed run type and payload explicit so chat cases can attach reply_to_run_id

Dataclass EvalCase:
- define one local evaluation example
- hold the run type, context, payload, response preferences, description, and optional seed run

Function default_model_refs:
- prefer the explicit ALL_MODELS environment list when it is configured
- build the default model matrix from current settings
- include the configured Gemini routing targets
- add a small OpenAI default set when an OpenAI key is configured
- remove duplicates while preserving order

Function parse_model_refs:
- accept explicit CLI model refs in provider:model format
- fall back to default_model_refs when no explicit list is provided

Function _parse_model_ref_strings:
- parse one or more provider:model strings into EvalModelRef records
- validate the format and deduplicate exact repeats while preserving order

Function build_eval_cases:
- generate the curated 5-example-per-feature local evaluation suite
- cover all six AI run types
- mix LoL and Wild Rift cases while respecting each game's slot contract

Function run_local_workflow_eval:
- execute every case against every requested model
- disable cache usage by always creating fresh runs
- collect per-case structured results plus latency/tokens/cost metadata
- aggregate average latency per feature/model
- write a human-readable markdown report to disk

Function render_markdown_report:
- turn the raw evaluation report payload into a manual-review-friendly markdown file
- include average latency summary and full per-case structured outputs

Function create_eval_app:
- reuse the normal FastAPI application wiring for local evaluation
- optionally mute verbose LLM debug logging for large evaluation runs

Function _run_one_case:
- execute one evaluation case for one model in an isolated database session
- optionally run a seed request first and pass reply_to_run_id into the target payload
- return either the completed run metadata + result or a failure record

Helper functions _summarize_results / _context / _slots / _runes / _context_brief:
- keep the report aggregation and case construction logic compact and game-aware
